[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "id": "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379",
      "db_id": 17592186124630,
      "title": "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ec2f7ffa-5605-580a-ad2a-05b34cb67daa",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is }\\text{invertible} \\\\ \\Updownarrow \\\\ \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{n} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\underline{\\phantom{WWWW}}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is a real $n\\times n$ matrix and $n$ is a positive integer. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following:\n\n*Let $A$ be a real $n\\times n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is }\\text{invertible} \\\\ \\Updownarrow \\\\ \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{n} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "44f1c4a7-d4cf-53f7-b509-329f03d11a16",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
